<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Euplectella aspergillum Turing wavenumber at 34.3 µm (Holocene, detail s0) — Code-to-model traceability: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring states the PDEs, the steady state, h, and λ_c. jacobian, sigma_of_k, integrate_amplitudes, and lattice_phi each implement one of those lines. The Lean file cites the same integers (343, 183183, 23²>120, equal-diffusion h<0, 1.48<λ ratio<1.49). Deduction: there is no equation number taken from Aizenberg et al. 2005, because that paper is anatomical rather than a dispersion-relation paper." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Euplectella aspergillum Turing wavenumber at 34.3 µm (Holocene, detail s0) — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The code implements the Schnakenberg Jacobian, the Turing inequality h²>4 D_u D_v det, σ(k) as the leading eigenvalue, and the critical-circle planform (axial, circumferential, two diagonals) that Aizenberg et al. 2005 describe as the square cage with diagonal ridges. Seven Lean theorems with zero sorry mirror the integer form of those statements. Deduction: the portrait is an amplitude-equation rendering, not a saturated two-dimensional PDE field, and Monn et al. 2015 layer thicknesses are not in the kinetics." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0.py L305–L332: amplitude ODE rather than a full 2D PDE saturation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/b9fc897b/models/2026-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L305-L332>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Euplectella aspergillum Turing wavenumber at 34.3 µm (Holocene, detail s0) — Morphometric validation: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dispersion goodness-of-fit is Pearson r=0.999989 and RMSE=0.00396 against σ(k), with an equal-diffusion negative control σ_max=−0.1025. The specimen mask has foreground fraction, aspect ratio, and circularity. The GIF crop versus the photograph gives radial-spectrum Pearson r=0.955, unit-vector RMSE=0.013, and orientation KS=0.075. Coherency is the weak term (0.192 versus 0.505). The image radial correlation is not above 0.98; the dispersion correlation is." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse-between-numerical-and-analytical-growth-rates>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-ablation-sigma-max-d-u-d-v-1-negative-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-gamma-sweep-wavelength-ratio-lambda-0-25-lambda-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-pinned-critical-wavelength-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-contour-circularity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-foreground-fraction-of-the-okeanos-photograph>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-orientation-histogram-ks-distance>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-radial-spectrum-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-simulation-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-turing-dispersion-pearson-r-of-numerical-versus-analytical-sigma-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Euplectella aspergillum Turing wavenumber at 34.3 µm (Holocene, detail s0) — MorphoEval overall 82.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Schnakenberg kinetics a=0.1, b=0.9, D_u=1, D_v=30, γ=1. Trace −0.2, det 1, h=23, h²=529>120, k_c²=23/60. The model unit is fixed so λ_c=3.43e-05 m (34.3 µm, log10=−4.465) and k_c=183183 m^-1. Age 0 Ma, chronoseries 1/1. Numerical growth rates versus σ(k) give Pearson r=0.999989, RMSE=0.00396 (n=10). Equal diffusion D_u=D_v=1 has h=−0.2 and σ_max=−0.1025. γ-sweep λ(0.25)/λ(1)=2. Four-mode amplitude equations tile a fan of tubes. Computer-vision similarity of the 12-frame 960×720 GIF against the Okeanos photograph is 81.8. Image radial Pearson is 0.955 and orientation KS is 0.075. Oscula alias into horizontal bands. Weighted rubric score 82.0/100. Not a pigment-ocellus model. Overall 82.0/100 (faithfulness 80.6, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b9fc897b; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/euplectella_aspergillum_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0.py at b9fc897b, image/png, 740881 B, 1848×644 px, artifact_sha256 e429d6680c5697a9a765bb933051748020f3a180a8530d7bd56c53c4552ecc30 (sha256 e429d6680c5697a9a765bb933051748020f3a180a8530d7bd56c53c4552ecc30), spec_fingerprint 124c45a3077f43da708d297825fc3db1c1d902225fd1e9032d50f5b8e2db9ef2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 124c45a3077f43da708d297825fc3db1c1d902225fd1e9032d50f5b8e2db9ef2; artifact_sha256: e429d6680c5697a9a765bb933051748020f3a180a8530d7bd56c53c4552ecc30. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Aizenberg et al. 2005: seven hierarchical levels and a cylindrical square lattice reinforced by diagonal ridges. | Weaver et al. 2007: assembly of the siliceous lattice of E. aspergillum. | Turing 1952: dispersion relation and critical wavenumber.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg linearisation and σ(k), calibrated to λ_c=3.43e-05 m. | Four-mode amplitude equations on |k|=k_c, drawn on a tube fan. | Equal-diffusion ablation and a γ sweep of wavelength.; transfer_boundary: The cohort phrase 'pigment stripe / ocellus' is transferred onto a skeletal lattice. The portrait magnifies λ_c; it is not a camera-scale micrograph.; does_not_claim: That this sponge has ocelli or pigment stripes. | That Monn et al. 2015 lamella thicknesses were fitted. | That the 51 µm sibling parameters were copied. | A chronospecies split. The series is Holocene only (0 Ma).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=1.9]: Portrait structure-tensor coherency is 0.192 against 0.505 on the photograph.",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.9]: Osculum rims alias the lattice into horizontal bands because arc length uses the local radius.",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Resample the circumferential coordinate at a fixed reference radius so the oscula stop aliasing into horizontal bands.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': \"Raise portrait/specimen structure-tensor coherency from 0.192 toward the photograph's 0.505 without pasting the photograph.\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Keep image radial Pearson (0.955) distinct from dispersion Pearson (0.999989). Do not treat the image correlation as having cleared 0.98 unless a re-measure shows it.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Second specimen. This pass uses one public-domain frame.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Independent second assessor. This pass is builder-scored.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Euplectella aspergillum Turing wavenumber at 34.3 µm (Holocene, detail s0) — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "γ in {0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} moves λ as 1/√γ (ratio λ(0.25)/λ(1) = 2 exactly) and the sequence is strictly decreasing. D_v in {12, 18, 24, 30, 40} is reported in the metrics JSON. Both orthogonal amplitudes remain positive at saturation, which is the square-lattice control. Display pitch lam_px is still a single visual choice, not a swept figure." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

